command: python3 -I -B <work>/defined_check.py <this script> (the program, written from this script's text, below; sha256 912d4b67762955a00799df0764a3a141db6536ec6bd7ca5ddb810ccacf83bc36), and the same over a copy of this script with one planted yn call and one planted is call of undefined helpers, and over a planted script that calls yn and is and defines neither (rulings Z, AD and AK a)
    """The defined-helper check (specs/0037: ruling Q, carried into each script's
    own shape block by ruling Z, widened by rulings AD and AK a): every helper
    a yn, ynnot, is or isnot call names is defined in the script, and each of
    the four the script calls is itself defined in it.
    
    Usage: python3 -I -B defined_check.py <script>
    
    A call's name is the word after a command substitution's opening, a dollar
    sign and a parenthesis, followed by one of the four names and a space,
    outside a comment line; a name is defined when a line of the script reads
    "<name>() {" (leading blanks allowed). The commands a script calls by name
    through them, "[", "cmp", "true" and "podman", are not helpers
    (gen/defined.py's list). Prints one line, "called <n>; undefined: <names or
    none>; yn defined: <yes|no|not called>; ynnot defined: ...; is defined:
    ...; isnot defined: ..."; exit 0 when no name is undefined and none of the
    four is called undefined, 1 otherwise, 2 on a usage or read error."""
    import re
    import sys
    
    COMMANDS = ("[", "cmp", "true", "podman")
    WRAPPERS = ("yn", "ynnot", "is", "isnot")
    CALL = re.compile(r"\$\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) ([^ )\"]+)")
    
    
    def main():
        if len(sys.argv) != 2:
            print("usage: defined_check.py <script>", file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(2)
        try:
            text = open(sys.argv[1], encoding="utf-8").read()
        except OSError as err:
            print("cannot read the script: %s" % err.strerror, file=sys.stderr)
            sys.exit(2)
        called, wrappers = set(), set()
        for line in text.split("\n"):
            if line.lstrip().startswith("#"):
                continue
            for wrapper, name in CALL.findall(line):
                wrappers.add(wrapper)
                called.add(name)
        defined = set(re.findall(r"^[ \t]*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\(\) \{", text, re.M))
        missing = sorted(n for n in called if n not in COMMANDS and n not in defined)
    
        def state(w):
            if w not in wrappers:
                return "not called"
            return "yes" if w in defined else "no"
        print("called %d; undefined: %s; %s"
              % (len(called), " ".join(missing) if missing else "none",
                 "; ".join("%s defined: %s" % (w, state(w)) for w in WRAPPERS)))
        bad = missing or any(state(w) == "no" for w in WRAPPERS)
        sys.exit(1 if bad else 0)
    
    
    main()
    called 143; undefined: none; yn defined: yes; ynnot defined: yes; is defined: not called; isnot defined: not called
